# Operations center (Famille B)

Epic: `docs/epics/EPIC-OPS-centre-operations.md`  
Estimator: `public/js/transfer-eta.js` (never invent download ETA)

## Famille A — dialogue (no Reduce, not in the center)

Create folder, rename, delete, share, properties, filters, move, text editor, media preview, bug report.

## Famille B — operation (OPS chrome required)

Upload+encrypt, ZIP extract (after submit), archive prepare, file download, archive download.

A Famille B modal must have: title, Reduce (once `running`), close, cancel (when `cancelSupported`), live resume via `taskId`.

## Non-negotiable

- Dismiss ≠ cancel. Esc / ✕ / backdrop while `running` opens `opsDismissModal` (Reduce / Stay / Cancel). Never `window.confirm()`.
- Header **Reduce** skips the mini-dialog (user already chose).
- Resume = `FilesOperations.resume(taskId)` → show the **same** modal + `executor.hydrate(task)`. Not an empty show.
- One Famille B modal visible at a time (except `opsDismissModal`).
- Listing downloads always go through `filesDownloadOperationModal` + `FilesDownloadLauncher` (grant + `/dl/*` Range). Never `FilesDownloadManager` / `download_progress_page` from the listing.
- Native download: `progressKnown=false`, no fake 0–100 bar, no in-page ETA.
- Cancel semantics are per type (encrypt/extract POST cancel + cleanup; archive prepare fail; download cannot abort Chrome after `handed_to_browser`).
- Purge all (`POST /files/operations/purge` + centre button): targets every non-`done` task; `handed_to_browser` is UI-only removal; never claim to abort Chrome downloads.
- ETA only through `TransferEta` when JS knows bytes.

